==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|restles}}, {{m|enm|restelees}}, from {{inh|en|ang|ræstlēas}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|rest|less}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|rĕstʹlĭs}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈɹɛstlɪs/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-restless.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{a|weak vowel}} {{IPA|en|/ˈɹɛstləs/}}
* {{hyph|en|rest|less}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Not allowing or affording [[rest]].
#: {{ux|en|The night before his wedding was a '''restless''' one.}}
# Without rest; unable to be [[still]] or [[quiet]]; [[uneasy]]; continually [[move|moving]].
#: {{ux|en|He was a '''restless''' child.}}
#: {{ux|en|She sat, '''restless''' and nervous, and tried to concentrate.}}
# Not satisfied to be at rest or in peace; [[averse]] to [[repose]]; eager for change; [[discontented]].
#: {{ux|en|A '''restless''' ambition.}}
# Deprived of rest or sleep.
#: {{ux|en|They remained '''restless''', sitting by the window the entire night.}}

====Synonyms====
{{checksense|en}}
* {{l|en|antsy}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|restless legs syndrome}}
* {{l|en|restlessly}}
* {{l|en|restlessness}}
* {{l|en|the natives are restless}}

